 "recognition_note": "The exact supplied VH/VL and all six CDRs occur in AU2022330406A1 (first public 2024-03-09), where Table 27 labels them ANTI-IL6RB; the patent defines IL6RB as gp130/CD130. This identifies the antibody target, not its epitope. No antibody-gp130 complex or pre-cutoff domain/residue map for this clone was recognized.",
 "what_separated_them": "No pre-cutoff line localizes this binder; the exact-sequence patent identifies gp130 only and is equally true of all nine candidates. The result is therefore a shallow prior over viable surfaces, not a concentrated epitope call. C3 leads because three independent Tier B axes converge: recurrent site-2 function, other-antibody/domain precedent, and measured glycan-clear positive/aromatic complementarity to this paratope. C6 follows on D4 precedent plus compact complementarity. C4 and C1 share D1 mass rather than providing independent confirmation; C4 gets the stronger share because a different Fab has a residue-level map there. Glycan proximity lowers C7 and C8, and lack of a named face function lowers C2, C8, and C9.",
